  "content_en": "7 Please be safe (1) It is really not an exaggeration to describe the struggle in the inner house as a war without gunpowder, especially in a large and complex family like the Wen family. The direct descendants are against the direct descendants, the direct descendants are against the concubines, the concubines are against the concubines... they are plotting against each other. If you are not careful, you may stand out and be cannon fodder, especially for an insignificant person like her. Sister Wenjiu straightened her back, lowered her head, and cheered up, but she did not forget to maintain a low profile on the outside, and followed closely behind Mr. Jiang. Wherever he looked, he could see Jiang's obviously relaxed and cautious steps. Sigh... Sister Ninth couldn't help but sigh in her heart. In this kind of situation, Mrs. Jiang must also be full of anxiety. She was originally a concubine's daughter-in-law, and she was born in a businessman, and her husband was still unreliable. She and the tenth sister's father, Wen Chonghu, took the exams for many years without success. Later, he donated a job, but he never had the opportunity to be promoted because of his lack of achievements. Now he is still a member of the fifth rank, living with a small salary. On the contrary, their elder brother, Wen Jingshui, the fourth young master of the Hou Mansion, is pretty good. He has just turned fourteen and has already passed the county and county examinations. He is just waiting to take the spring examination next spring. This is still the most progressive among the brothers of the Wen family, so he received special care from the old lady. He temporarily skipped all morning and evening greetings and only read books in the yard. The son's future made Jiang family somewhat respectable in front of the Wen family, but at the same time it also attracted a lot of jealousy... \"Third wife, ninth girl, tenth girl, please come in quickly!\" As soon as they walked into the door, a pretty maid in a crimson cotton gauze coat came out and raised the curtain for them. It was Cuifeng, the eldest maid next to the old lady. \"Thank you, Miss Cuifeng.\" Mrs. Jiang smiled at Cuifeng, and Sister Ten and Sister Ninth also nodded to Cuifeng. \"Sister Cuifeng, this gown is so moist and beautiful!\" Cui Qiao, who was following Mr. Jiang, took Cuifeng's hand affectionately and secretly pushed a silver nudity into her. Cuifeng was startled, and his expression soon returned to normal, and then he said to Cuiqiao, \"What does it look like? It's just a fresh coat, it's brand new, and the color fades after a wash...\" At this point, he suddenly covered his sleeves and smiled again, \"Well... sister, you have the same vision as the second wife and the fourth wife.\" \"Really?\" Cui Qiao heard this and was immediately surprised. Ms. Jiang, who was inside and outside the door, was slightly startled, then she straightened her chest and raised her head, then tugged on her smooth, wrinkle-free clothes and went in. Of course Sister Jiu saw all this and couldn't help but shake her head secretly in her heart. I'm afraid her aunt's heart is no less nervous than hers, right? Otherwise, there would be no need to exchange money for such a message... The cold wind was howling outside, but the interior was as warm as spring - through the clear glass window on the rosewood inlaid ivory japanese fan, Sister Wenjiu's eyes fell on the old woman sitting on the big Kang with huanghuali cloud head, surrounded by everyone. She has a long face, a head full of silver hair that is meticulously combed, and wears an amber chinchilla leather jacket with front sleeves and a black iron skirt. She is the most powerful and senior person in the Hou family - Mrs. Li. Sister Jiu had a good impression of Taijun Li, although Taijun Li's eyes rarely fell on her, and sometimes he glanced around her body, which was indifferent. There are many descendants, but he is not outstanding. In the eyes of this old man, he is just like a passerby. But she has never treated herself lightly, and her treatment is the same as that of the sisters in the Wen family. This is enough. She has always been a grateful and contented person... \"...What's wrong with the fourth grandma's touch? Could it be that only the great-grandmother can touch it, and the fourth grandma can't...\" \"Fourth brother and sister, why are you competing with a child? I'm not protecting the calf, it's just him. You are so old, you are less than a week and a half under the age of 18, what do you know... Yunyue, take Brother Bao out for a breather, otherwise he will start crying again and again...\" Suddenly a voice full of displeasure and boredom mixed with the sobbing of a child rang out, and then a beautiful woman with a flowing bun quickly came out holding a little boy with a pouty mouth and tears in his arms. \"Hello, third aunt!\" The woman met the Jiang family and the others, and immediately greeted the Jiang family. \"Well, Yunyue, what's going on?\" Mrs. Jiang looked at the woman, then at the little boy. \"What else can I do...\" The woman pouted unhappily at the person behind her, but she didn't say much. Her eyes fell on the Ninth Sister and the Tenth Sister behind Jiang. \"I've met my sister-in-law!\" Sister Ninth quickly pulled Sister Ten to salute her. The man in front of me is the second husbandThe daughter-in-law of Wen Chongnian, the eldest son of the Miao family, was from a prominent family in the south of the Yangtze River. She had a clever mouth and was good at speaking. This Feng family was just like the second wife back then. Within a year of marrying into the Wen family, she got a boy and gave birth to the eldest grandson of the Hou family. For this reason, she won the heart of the old lady, and the son she gave birth to, Brother Bao, was even more in the heart of the old lady. \"The ninth sister and the tenth sister really changed every day, each one became more and more beautiful.\" Feng immediately looked at the two sisters and smiled affectionately. The two sisters lowered their heads in shame. \"I'll talk to the third aunt and sisters another day. I'm leaving first.\" Seeing Brother Bao in her arms, Mrs. Feng began to curl her lips and cry again, and left in a hurry. \"Fourth family member, I'm not telling you, your daughter-in-law will be old in a few years, why don't you know it's more prudent...\" Several people entered the inner room and heard Li Taijun scolding a woman beside them. The woman was wearing a half-worn lilac-colored gown with a silk gourd pattern. She was well made, but her cheekbones were a bit high, and she looked mean. She was Zhen, the wife of Wen Chonghu, the fourth master of the Hou Mansion. This Zhen family also comes from a famous family, but unfortunately she is a concubine. Originally a concubine, she married a concubine, with a low status, a shabby dowry, and many disappointments. Her temperament gradually became a little arrogant and unruly, and it was inevitable to be annoying. \"What the old lady taught me is that my daughter-in-law must have changed. Don't be angry!\" After being scolded by the old lady, Mrs. Zhen quickly bowed her head and admitted her mistake. The old lady didn't say anything, she just took the tea handed over by Cuiping with a cold face. The woman on the other side of the old lady, wearing a muddy gold-stained flowered turban and a proud temperament, curled her lips in disdain. This woman is Miao, the wife of the second master Wen Chonghe. She is of noble birth and can please the old lady. She is the most favored daughter-in-law in front of the old lady. Being left hanging in the middle of the room in front of all the junior servants, Zhen was so angry that her teeth were almost broken, and she secretly hated the old lady's partiality. Didn't she just touch Brother Bao? I didn't expect that that little naughty person could be so snobbish with such a small obstacle, and that this old pious woman was so partial, which made her so angry! However... the fourth bedroom still relied on the old godly woman and the second bedroom for all matters, so she could only swallow her anger. Embarrassed and angry, her eyes suddenly fell on Mrs. Jiang who had just walked in. She turned her eyes instantly and smiled, \"Third sister-in-law, you are here. I thought the old lady not only spared your fourth son's greetings, but also yours.\" Her words made Mrs. Jiang's expression change, and the ninth sister also frowned instantly. Human nature is really despicable. For the sake of oneself, he will not hesitate to trample on others... --------- Digression - - It's even later, I went too far, sorry! Happy New Year, folks!",
